  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Learning Facilitator Programmatic Approach for Sustainable Economic Development (PADEO) Tunisia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The inception phase of Programmatic Approach for Sustainable Economic Development (PADEO) in Tunisia has been completed, and the Embassy in Tunis is now about to enter the implementation phase. During this phase, the partners will use a reflexive monitoring approach, which emphasizes learning from both actions and from each other. The goal of reflexive monitoring is to continuously make adjustments based on lessons learned, always with the ultimate objective systemic impact in mind. Rather than focusing solely on what is happening, the partners will also explore how and why things are happening. This process-focused approach helps to better understand the complexity of the systemic change we envision, and take appropriate actions to reach it. By testing what works and what doesn&apos;t, the partners can continually improve their decisions, policies, and practices and achieve better results.An external learning facilitator, who can guide the reflexive monitoring process, will ensure that there is sufficient capacity to continuously learn throughout the process.</narrative>
  </description>
